  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "If \\(N\\gt1,\\) then \\[ \\sqrt[3]{N\\sqrt[3]{N\\sqrt[3]{N}}}= \\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(N^{\\frac{1}{27}}\\)",
    "B": "\\(N^{\\frac{1}{9}}\\)",
    "C": "\\(N^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\)",
    "D": "\\(N^{\\frac{13}{27}}\\)",
    "E": "\\(N\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Work from the innermost cube root outward. Since \\(N>1\\), all bases are positive: multiplying powers of \\(N\\) adds their exponents, and taking a cube root divides the exponent by \\(3\\).\n\nThe innermost root is \\(\\sqrt[3]{N}=N^{1/3}\\). The next root is\n\\[\n\\sqrt[3]{N\\cdot N^{1/3}}\n=N^{(1+1/3)/3}\n=N^{4/9}.\n\\]\nTherefore the entire expression is\n\\[\n\\sqrt[3]{N\\cdot N^{4/9}}\n=N^{(1+4/9)/3}\n=N^{13/27}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(N^{13/27}\\), choice D.",
